{"id":"mahabharata-3-061","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":61,"title":"एकषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 61 · Damayanti's wanderings","summary":{"en":"Damayanti wanders through the terrible forest calling to mountains, trees and beasts for news of Nala. She visits a hermitage whose sages foretell her reunion and then vanish, and joins a caravan of merchants bound for the kingdom of Chedi.","kn":"ದಮಯಂತಿ ಭಯಂಕರ ಕಾಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಪರ್ವತ, ಮರ, ಮೃಗಗಳನ್ನು ನಳನ ಸುದ್ದಿ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾ ಅಲೆಯುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಒಂದು ಆಶ್ರಮದ ಋಷಿಗಳು ಪುನರ್ಮಿಲನವನ್ನು ಭವಿಷ್ಯ ನುಡಿದು ಮಾಯವಾಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅವಳು ಚೇದಿರಾಜ್ಯಕ್ಕೆ ಹೋಗುವ ವ್ಯಾಪಾರಿಗಳ ತಂಡವನ್ನು ಸೇರುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"दमयन्ती भयंकर वन में पर्वतों, वृक्षों और पशुओं से नल का समाचार पूछती भटकती हैं। एक आश्रम के ऋषि उनके पुनर्मिलन की भविष्यवाणी कर अन्तर्धान हो जाते हैं, और वे चेदि राज्य जा रहे व्यापारियों के काफ़िले में मिल जाती हैं।","te":"దమయంతి భయంకర అడవిలో పర్వతాలను, చెట్లను, మృగాలను నలుని గురించి అడుగుతూ తిరుగుతుంది. ఒక ఆశ్రమంలోని ఋషులు పునర్మిలనాన్ని జోస్యం చెప్పి అదృశ్యమవుతారు; ఆమె చేది రాజ్యానికి వెళ్తున్న వర్తకుల బిడారులో చేరుతుంది.","ta":"தமயந்தி கொடிய காட்டில் மலைகள், மரங்கள், விலங்குகளிடம் நளனைப் பற்றிக் கேட்டபடி அலைகிறாள். ஓர் ஆசிரம முனிவர்கள் மீண்டும் இணைவதை முன்னுரைத்து மறைய, அவள் சேதி நாட்டுக்குச் செல்லும் வணிகர் கூட்டத்துடன் சேர்கிறாள்.","ml":"ദമയന്തി ഭീകരമായ കാട്ടിലൂടെ അലയുന്നു; പർവതങ്ങളോടും മരങ്ങളോടും മൃഗങ്ങളോടും നളനെക്കുറിച്ച് ചോദിച്ച് വിളിച്ചുപറയുന്നു. ഒരു ആശ്രമത്തിൽ എത്തുന്ന അവൾക്ക് അവിടത്തെ മുനിമാർ പുനഃസമാഗമം പ്രവചിച്ച് പിന്നെ മറയുന്നു; അവൾ ചേദിരാജ്യത്തേക്ക് പോകുന്ന വ്യാപാരികളുടെ സംഘത്തിൽ ചേരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.61; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"इन्द्रलोकाभिगमनपर्व","titleEn":"Indralokabhigamana Parva (Journey to Indra's world)","verses":[{"text":"बृहदश्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brihadashva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"सा निहत्य मृगव्याधं प्रतस्थे कमलेक्षणा ।\nवनं प्रतिभयं शून्यं झिल्लिकागणनादितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed the deer-hunter, the lotus-eyed woman went on, into a fearsome, empty forest loud with swarms of crickets."}},{"n":2,"text":"सिंहव्याघ्रवराहर्क्षरुरुद्वीपिनिषेवितम् ।\nनानापक्षिगणाकीर्णं म्लेच्छतस्करसेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was haunted by lions, tigers, boars, bears, ruru deer and leopards, filled with flocks of birds of many kinds, and frequented by barbarians and thieves."}},{"n":3,"text":"शालवेणुधवाश्वत्थतिन्दुकेङ्गुदकिंशुकैः ।\nअर्जुनारिष्टसंछन्नं चन्दनैश्च सशाल्मलैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was covered with sala, bamboo, dhava, peepal, tinduka, ingudi and kimshuka trees, with arjuna and arishta, sandalwood and silk-cotton trees."}},{"n":4,"text":"जम्ब्वाम्रलोध्रखदिरशाकवेत्रसमाकुलम् ।\nकाश्मर्यामलकप्लक्षकदम्बोदुम्बरावृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was thick with jambu, mango, lodhra, khadira, teak and cane, and surrounded by kashmarya, amalaka, plaksha, kadamba and udumbara trees."}},{"n":5,"text":"बदरीबिल्वसंछन्नं न्यग्रोधैश्च समाकुलम् ।\nप्रियालतालखर्जूरहरीतकबिभीतकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was covered with jujube and bilva, crowded with banyans, with priyala, palmyra, date, haritaki and vibhitaka trees."}},{"n":6,"text":"नानाधातुशतैर्नद्धान्विविधानपि चाचलान् ।\nनिकुञ्जान्पक्षिसंघुष्टान्दरीश्चाद्भुतदर्शनाः ।\nनदीः सरांसि वापीश्च विविधांश्च मृगद्विजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were hills streaked with hundreds of mineral colors, bowers loud with birds, wondrous-looking caves, rivers, lakes, pools, and many kinds of animals and birds."}},{"n":7,"text":"सा बहून्भीमरूपांश्च पिशाचोरगराक्षसान् ।\nपल्वलानि तडागानि गिरिकूटानि सर्वशः ।\nसरितः सागरांश्चैव ददर्शाद्भुतदर्शनान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She saw many fearsome shapes, pishachas, serpents and rakshasas, ponds, tanks, mountain peaks everywhere, and rivers and lakes of wondrous look."}},{"n":8,"text":"यूथशो ददृशे चात्र विदर्भाधिपनन्दिनी ।\nमहिषान्वराहान्गोमायूनृक्षवानरपन्नगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The daughter of the Vidarbha king saw there herds of buffalo, boars, jackals, bears, monkeys and snakes."}},{"n":9,"text":"तेजसा यशसा स्थित्या श्रिया च परया युता ।\nवैदर्भी विचरत्येका नलमन्वेषती तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Endowed with splendor, fame, steadiness and supreme beauty, the Vidarbha princess wandered alone then, searching for Nala."}},{"n":10,"text":"नाबिभ्यत्सा नृपसुता भैमी तत्राथ कस्यचित् ।\nदारुणामटवीं प्राप्य भर्तृव्यसनकर्शिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though she had reached that terrible wilderness, wasted by her husband's misfortune, Bhima's royal daughter feared nothing there."}},{"n":11,"text":"विदर्भतनया राजन्विललाप सुदुःखिता ।\nभर्तृशोकपरीताङ्गी शिलातलसमाश्रिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, the Vidarbha princess, sitting on a flat rock with her body overcome by grief for her husband, lamented in great misery."}},{"text":"दमयन्त्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Damayanti said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"सिंहोरस्क महाबाहो निषधानां जनाधिप ।\nक्व नु राजन्गतोऽसीह त्यक्त्वा मां निर्जने वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Lion-chested, mighty-armed lord of the Nishadhas, where have you gone, king, leaving me in this empty forest?"}},{"n":13,"text":"अश्वमेधादिभिर्वीर क्रतुभिः स्वाप्तदक्षिणैः ।\nकथमिष्ट्वा नरव्याघ्र मयि मिथ्या प्रवर्तसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hero, after performing sacrifices like the Ashvamedha with ample fees, tiger among men, how can you be false to me?"}},{"n":14,"text":"यत्त्वयोक्तं नरव्याघ्र मत्समक्षं महाद्युते ।\nकर्तुमर्हसि कल्याण तदृतं पार्थिवर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"What you said, tiger among men, brilliant one, in my presence, noble bull among kings, you ought to make true."}},{"n":15,"text":"यथोक्तं विहगैर्हंसैः समीपे तव भूमिप ।\nमत्सकाशे च तैरुक्तं तदवेक्षितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"What the swans, those birds, said near you, lord of earth, and also said to me, you should bear in mind."}},{"n":16,"text":"चत्वार एकतो वेदाः साङ्गोपाङ्गाः सविस्तराः ।\nस्वधीता मानवश्रेष्ठ सत्यमेकं किलैकतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The four Vedas with their limbs and subsidiary parts, well studied, best of men, are weighed against truth alone on the other side."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्मादर्हसि शत्रुघ्न सत्यं कर्तुं नरेश्वर ।\nउक्तवानसि यद्वीर मत्सकाशे पुरा वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, slayer of foes, lord of men, you ought to make true the word you spoke to me before, hero."}},{"n":18,"text":"हा वीर ननु नामाहमिष्टा किल तवानघ ।\nअस्यामटव्यां घोरायां किं मां न प्रतिभाषसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alas, hero, was I not your beloved, blameless one? In this dreadful forest, why do you not answer me?"}},{"n":19,"text":"भर्त्सयत्येष मां रौद्रो व्यात्तास्यो दारुणाकृतिः ।\nअरण्यराट्क्षुधाविष्टः किं मां न त्रातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"This fierce king of the forest, with gaping mouth and dreadful form, is threatening me, driven by hunger; do you not protect me?"}},{"n":20,"text":"न मे त्वदन्या सुभगे प्रिया इत्यब्रवीस्तदा ।\nतामृतां कुरु कल्याण पुरोक्तां भारतीं नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"You said then, 'I have no beloved other than you, fair one.' Make that earlier promise true, king."}},{"n":21,"text":"उन्मत्तां विलपन्तीं मां भार्यामिष्टां नराधिप ।\nईप्सितामीप्सितो नाथ किं मां न प्रतिभाषसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am your loved wife, lord of men, crying out like one mad, and wished for by you as you were by me; why do you not answer?"}},{"n":22,"text":"कृशां दीनां विवर्णां च मलिनां वसुधाधिप ।\nवस्त्रार्धप्रावृतामेकां विलपन्तीमनाथवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thin, wretched, pale and dirty, wearing half a garment, alone, lamenting like one with no protector,"}},{"n":23,"text":"यूथभ्रष्टामिवैकां मां हरिणीं पृथुलोचन ।\nन मानयसि मानार्ह रुदतीमरिकर्शन ॥","meaning":{"en":"like a doe separated from her herd, wide-eyed one, you do not heed me as I weep, though you deserve honor, scourge of foes."}},{"n":24,"text":"महाराज महारण्ये मामिहैकाकिनीं सतीम् ।\nआभाषमाणां स्वां पत्नीं किं मां न प्रतिभाषसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, alone in this great forest, speaking to you as your own wife, why do you not answer me?"}},{"n":25,"text":"कुलशीलोपसंपन्नं चारुसर्वाङ्गशोभनम् ।\nनाद्य त्वामनुपश्यामि गिरावस्मिन्नरोत्तम ।\nवने चास्मिन्महाघोरे सिंहव्याघ्रनिषेविते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of men, noble in birth and conduct, beautiful in every limb, I do not see you today on this mountain or in this dreadful forest haunted by lions and tigers,"}},{"n":26,"text":"शयानमुपविष्टं वा स्थितं वा निषधाधिप ।\nप्रस्थितं वा नरश्रेष्ठ मम शोकविवर्धन ॥","meaning":{"en":"whether lying, sitting, standing or walking, lord of the Nishadhas, you who increase my grief."}},{"n":27,"text":"कं नु पृच्छामि दुःखार्ता त्वदर्थे शोककर्शिता ।\nकच्चिद्दृष्टस्त्वयारण्ये संगत्येह नलो नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whom shall I ask, afflicted and wasted by sorrow for your sake: Have you seen King Nala here in the forest?"}},{"n":28,"text":"को नु मे कथयेदद्य वनेऽस्मिन्विष्ठितं नलम् ।\nअभिरूपं महात्मानं परव्यूहविनाशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who will tell me today where Nala, handsome, great-souled destroyer of enemy ranks, is in this forest?"}},{"n":29,"text":"यमन्वेषसि राजानं नलं पद्मनिभेक्षणम् ।\nअयं स इति कस्याद्य श्रोष्यामि मधुरां गिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king you look for, Nala, lotus-eyed: who will say, 'Here he is,' so that I may hear that sweet voice today?"}},{"n":30,"text":"अरण्यराडयं श्रीमांश्चतुर्दंष्ट्रो महाहनुः ।\nशार्दूलोऽभिमुखः प्रैति पृच्छाम्येनमशङ्किता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here comes the king of the forest, a fine tiger with four fangs and huge jaws, facing me; I will ask him without fear."}},{"n":31,"text":"भवान्मृगाणामधिपस्त्वमस्मिन्कानने प्रभुः ।\nविदर्भराजतनयां दमयन्तीति विद्धि माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are the lord of beasts, the master in this forest. Know me as Damayanti, daughter of the king of Vidarbha,"}},{"n":32,"text":"निषधाधिपतेर्भार्यां नलस्यामित्रघातिनः ।\nपतिमन्वेषतीमेकां कृपणां शोककर्शिताम् ।\nआश्वासय मृगेन्द्रेह यदि दृष्टस्त्वया नलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"wife of Nala, the king of the Nishadhas and slayer of his foes, searching for her husband, alone, wretched, wasted by grief. Comfort me, lord of beasts, if you have seen Nala."}},{"n":33,"text":"अथ वारण्यनृपते नलं यदि न शंससि ।\nमामदस्व मृगश्रेष्ठ विशोकां कुरु दुःखिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or if, king of the forest, you do not tell me of Nala, then devour me, best of beasts, and free me, the unhappy, from sorrow."}},{"n":34,"text":"श्रुत्वारण्ये विलपितं ममैष मृगराट्स्वयम् ।\nयात्येतां मृष्टसलिलामापगां सागरंगमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard my lament in the wilderness, this king of beasts himself goes to this stream of clear water flowing to the sea."}},{"n":35,"text":"इमं शिलोच्चयं पुण्यं शृङ्गैर्बहुभिरुच्छ्रितैः ।\nविराजद्भिर्दिवस्पृग्भिर्नैकवर्णैर्मनोरमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This holy mountain, with its many lofty, shining, sky-touching peaks of many colors and lovely,"}},{"n":36,"text":"नानाधातुसमाकीर्णं विविधोपलभूषितम् ।\nअस्यारण्यस्य महतः केतुभूतमिवोच्छ्रितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"strewn with many minerals, adorned with various rocks, towering like the banner of this great forest,"}},{"n":37,"text":"सिंहशार्दूलमातङ्गवराहर्क्षमृगायुतम् ।\nपतत्रिभिर्बहुविधैः समन्तादनुनादितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"swarming with lions, tigers, elephants, boars, bears and deer, and resounding all around with many kinds of birds,"}},{"n":38,"text":"किंशुकाशोकबकुलपुंनागैरुपशोभितम् ।\nसरिद्भिः सविहंगाभिः शिखरैश्चोपशोभितम् ।\nगिरिराजमिमं तावत्पृच्छामि नृपतिं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"adorned with kimshuka, ashoka, bakula and punnaga trees, with rivers and birds and with peaks: this king of mountains I will ask about the king."}},{"n":39,"text":"भगवन्नचलश्रेष्ठ दिव्यदर्शन विश्रुत ।\nशरण्य बहुकल्याण नमस्तेऽस्तु महीधर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Blessed best of mountains, divine in sight and famed, giver of refuge, full of blessings, I bow to you, upholder of the earth."}},{"n":40,"text":"प्रणमे त्वाभिगम्याहं राजपुत्रीं निबोध माम् ।\nराज्ञः स्नुषां राजभार्यां दमयन्तीति विश्रुताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I come to you and bow; know me as a king's daughter, a king's daughter-in-law and a king's wife, known as Damayanti."}},{"n":41,"text":"राजा विदर्भाधिपतिः पिता मम महारथः ।\nभीमो नाम क्षितिपतिश्चातुर्वर्ण्यस्य रक्षिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"My father is the king of Vidarbha, a great chariot-warrior named Bhima, protector of the four classes, a lord of earth,"}},{"n":42,"text":"राजसूयाश्वमेधानां क्रतूनां दक्षिणावताम् ।\nआहर्ता पार्थिवश्रेष्ठः पृथुचार्वञ्चितेक्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"performer of the Rajasuya and Ashvamedha sacrifices with generous fees, the best of kings, with broad and beautiful eyes,"}},{"n":43,"text":"ब्रह्मण्यः साधुवृत्तश्च सत्यवागनसूयकः ।\nशीलवान्सुसमाचारः पृथुश्रीर्धर्मविच्छुचिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"devoted to brahmins, upright, truthful, free of envy, virtuous, well behaved, of great fortune, knowing dharma and pure,"}},{"n":44,"text":"सम्यग्गोप्ता विदर्भाणां निर्जितारिगणः प्रभुः ।\nतस्य मां विद्धि तनयां भगवंस्त्वामुपस्थिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"rightly protecting the Vidarbhas, a lord who has conquered his foes. Know me, blessed one, as his daughter come to you."}},{"n":45,"text":"निषधेषु महाशैल श्वशुरो मे नृपोत्तमः ।\nसुगृहीतनामा विख्यातो वीरसेन इति स्म ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great mountain, my father-in-law is the best of kings among the Nishadhas, rightly named and renowned, Virasena."}},{"n":46,"text":"तस्य राज्ञः सुतो वीरः श्रीमान्सत्यपराक्रमः ।\nक्रमप्राप्तं पितुः स्वं यो राज्यं समनुशास्ति ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king's son, a hero, glorious and truly valiant, who rules his father's kingdom in succession,"}},{"n":47,"text":"नलो नामारिदमनः पुण्यश्लोक इति श्रुतः ।\nब्रह्मण्यो वेदविद्वाग्मी पुण्यकृत्सोमपोऽग्निचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"is named Nala, subduer of foes, known as of holy fame, devoted to brahmins, learned in the Vedas, eloquent, a doer of good, a soma-drinker and fire-piler."}},{"n":48,"text":"यष्टा दाता च योद्धा च सम्यक्चैव प्रशासिता ।\nतस्य मामचलश्रेष्ठ विद्धि भार्यामिहागताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A sacrificer, a giver, a warrior and a good ruler: know me, best of mountains, as his wife, come here"}},{"n":49,"text":"त्यक्तश्रियं भर्तृहीनामनाथां व्यसनान्विताम् ।\nअन्वेषमाणां भर्तारं तं वै नरवरोत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"bereft of wealth, without a husband, without protection, in distress, searching for that best of men, my husband."}},{"n":50,"text":"खमुल्लिखद्भिरेतैर्हि त्वया शृङ्गशतैर्नृपः ।\nकच्चिद्दृष्टोऽचलश्रेष्ठ वनेऽस्मिन्दारुणे नलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With these hundreds of peaks scratching the sky, have you seen that king Nala, best of mountains, in this dreadful forest?"}},{"n":51,"text":"गजेन्द्रविक्रमो धीमान्दीर्घबाहुरमर्षणः ।\nविक्रान्तः सत्यवाग्धीरो भर्ता मम महायशाः ।\nनिषधानामधिपतिः कच्चिद्दृष्टस्त्वया नलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wise, long-armed, easily angered, valiant, truthful, steady, my glorious husband with an elephant's stride, lord of the Nishadhas: have you seen Nala?"}},{"n":52,"text":"किं मां विलपतीमेकां पर्वतश्रेष्ठ दुःखिताम् ।\nगिरा नाश्वासयस्यद्य स्वां सुतामिव दुःखिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Why, best of mountains, do you not comfort me today with a word, lamenting alone in my sorrow, as if I were your own daughter in grief?"}},{"n":53,"text":"वीर विक्रान्त धर्मज्ञ सत्यसंध महीपते ।\nयद्यस्यस्मिन्वने राजन्दर्शयात्मानमात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hero, valiant, knowing dharma, true to your pledge, lord of earth, if you are in this forest, king, show yourself."}},{"n":54,"text":"कदा नु स्निग्धगम्भीरां जीमूतस्वनसंनिभाम् ।\nश्रोष्यामि नैषधस्याहं वाचं ताममृतोपमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When shall I hear the Nishadha's voice, gentle, deep, like the rumble of a cloud, like nectar,"}},{"n":55,"text":"वैदर्भीत्येव कथितां शुभां राज्ञो महात्मनः ।\nआम्नायसारिणीमृद्धां मम शोकनिबर्हिणीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"saying 'Vaidarbhi,' that fine voice of the great king, true to the scriptures, full and the destroyer of my sorrow?\""}},{"n":56,"text":"इति सा तं गिरिश्रेष्ठमुक्त्वा पार्थिवनन्दिनी ।\nदमयन्ती ततो भूयो जगाम दिशमुत्तराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So saying to that best of mountains, the king's daughter Damayanti went on in the northern direction."}},{"n":57,"text":"सा गत्वा त्रीनहोरात्रान्ददर्श परमाङ्गना ।\nतापसारण्यमतुलं दिव्यकाननदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After going three days and nights, that excellent woman saw a peerless forest of ascetics, like a divine woodland."}},{"n":58,"text":"वसिष्ठभृग्वत्रिसमैस्तापसैरुपशोभितम् ।\nनियतैः संयताहारैर्दमशौचसमन्वितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was adorned with ascetics equal to Vasishtha, Bhrigu and Atri, disciplined, restrained in food, self-controlled and pure,"}},{"n":59,"text":"अब्भक्षैर्वायुभक्षैश्च पत्राहारैस्तथैव च ।\nजितेन्द्रियैर्महाभागैः स्वर्गमार्गदिदृक्षुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"some living on water, some on air, some on leaves, masters of their senses, greatly fortunate, wishing to see the path to heaven."}},{"n":60,"text":"वल्कलाजिनसंवीतैर्मुनिभिः संयतेन्द्रियैः ।\nतापसाध्युषितं रम्यं ददर्शाश्रममण्डलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She saw a lovely circle of hermitages inhabited by ascetics, sages clad in bark and skins and with restrained senses."}},{"n":61,"text":"सा दृष्ट्वैवाश्रमपदं नानामृगनिषेवितम् ।\nशाखामृगगणैश्चैव तापसैश्च समन्वितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that hermitage, frequented by many animals and filled with troops of monkeys and ascetics,"}},{"n":62,"text":"सुभ्रूः सुकेशी सुश्रोणी सुकुचा सुद्विजानना ।\nवर्चस्विनी सुप्रतिष्ठा स्वञ्चितोद्यतगामिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"she, with fine brows, hair, hips, breasts and teeth, radiant, steady, and graceful in her walk,"}},{"n":63,"text":"सा विवेशाश्रमपदं वीरसेनसुतप्रिया ।\nयोषिद्रत्नं महाभागा दमयन्ती मनस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"the beloved of Virasena's son, a jewel among women, the greatly fortunate and spirited Damayanti, entered the hermitage."}},{"n":64,"text":"साभिवाद्य तपोवृद्धान्विनयावनता स्थिता ।\nस्वागतं त इति प्रोक्ता तैः सर्वैस्तापसैश्च सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"She greeted the elders in austerity and stood humbly bowed, and all those ascetics welcomed her."}},{"n":65,"text":"पूजां चास्या यथान्यायं कृत्वा तत्र तपोधनाः ।\nआस्यतामित्यथोचुस्ते ब्रूहि किं करवामहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having honored her properly, those rich in austerity said, \"Be seated. Tell us, what can we do?\""}},{"n":66,"text":"तानुवाच वरारोहा कच्चिद्भगवतामिह ।\nतपस्यग्निषु धर्मेषु मृगपक्षिषु चानघाः ।\nकुशलं वो महाभागाः स्वधर्मचरणेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fine lady said to them: \"Blameless blessed ones, is all well with you in austerity, in the sacred fires, in dharma, among the beasts and birds, and in following your own duties?\""}},{"n":67,"text":"तैरुक्ता कुशलं भद्रे सर्वत्रेति यशस्विनी ।\nब्रूहि सर्वानवद्याङ्गि का त्वं किं च चिकीर्षसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"They answered, \"It is well everywhere, good lady. Tell us all, faultless one: who are you and what do you wish to do?"}},{"n":68,"text":"दृष्ट्वैव ते परं रूपं द्युतिं च परमामिह ।\nविस्मयो नः समुत्पन्नः समाश्वसिहि मा शुचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing your supreme beauty and brilliance, wonder has arisen in us. Take comfort and do not grieve."}},{"n":69,"text":"अस्यारण्यस्य महती देवता वा महीभृतः ।\nअस्या नु नद्याः कल्याणि वद सत्यमनिन्दिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell us truly, blameless one: are you the great goddess of this forest, or of this mountain, or of this river?\""}},{"n":70,"text":"साब्रवीत्तानृषीन्नाहमरण्यस्यास्य देवता ।\nन चाप्यस्य गिरेर्विप्रा न नद्या देवताप्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She said to the sages: \"I am not the goddess of this forest, nor of the mountain, nor of the river, brahmins."}},{"n":71,"text":"मानुषीं मां विजानीत यूयं सर्वे तपोधनाः ।\nविस्तरेणाभिधास्यामि तन्मे शृणुत सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know me as a human woman, all you rich in austerity. I will tell you in detail; please all listen to me."}},{"n":72,"text":"विदर्भेषु महीपालो भीमो नाम महाद्युतिः ।\nतस्य मां तनयां सर्वे जानीत द्विजसत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In Vidarbha there is a king named Bhima, of great splendor. Know me, best of brahmins, as his daughter."}},{"n":73,"text":"निषधाधिपतिर्धीमान्नलो नाम महायशाः ।\nवीरः संग्रामजिद्विद्वान्मम भर्ता विशां पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"My husband, lord of people, is the wise Nishadha king named Nala of great fame, a hero, a conqueror in battle, learned."}},{"n":74,"text":"देवताभ्यर्चनपरो द्विजातिजनवत्सलः ।\nगोप्ता निषधवंशस्य महाभागो महाद्युतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devoted to worship of the gods, fond of brahmins, protector of the Nishadha line, greatly fortunate and brilliant,"}},{"n":75,"text":"सत्यवाग्धर्मवित्प्राज्ञः सत्यसंधोऽरिमर्दनः ।\nब्रह्मण्यो दैवतपरः श्रीमान्परपुरंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"truthful, knowing dharma, wise, true to his word, crusher of foes, devoted to brahmins and the gods, glorious, conqueror of enemy cities,"}},{"n":76,"text":"नलो नाम नृपश्रेष्ठो देवराजसमद्युतिः ।\nमम भर्ता विशालाक्षः पूर्णेन्दुवदनोऽरिहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"that best of kings, named Nala, as radiant as the king of gods, large-eyed, with a face like the full moon, slayer of foes, is my husband."}},{"n":77,"text":"आहर्ता क्रतुमुख्यानां वेदवेदाङ्गपारगः ।\nसपत्नानां मृधे हन्ता रविसोमसमप्रभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is a performer of the foremost sacrifices, master of the Vedas and their limbs, killer of rivals in battle, with a brilliance like the sun and moon."}},{"n":78,"text":"स कैश्चिन्निकृतिप्रज्ञैरकल्याणैर्नराधमैः ।\nआहूय पृथिवीपालः सत्यधर्मपरायणः ।\nदेवने कुशलैर्जिह्मैर्जितो राज्यं वसूनि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some crooked, ill-meaning lowest of men, skilled in deceit, called that king, devoted to truth and dharma, to a game of dice, and being expert and cunning at gaming, they won his kingdom and wealth."}},{"n":79,"text":"तस्य मामवगच्छध्वं भार्यां राजर्षभस्य वै ।\nदमयन्तीति विख्यातां भर्तृदर्शनलालसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know me as the wife of that bull among kings, famed as Damayanti, eager to see my husband."}},{"n":80,"text":"सा वनानि गिरींश्चैव सरांसि सरितस्तथा ।\nपल्वलानि च रम्याणि तथारण्यानि सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wander here in sorrow through forests, mountains, lakes, rivers, lovely pools and woodlands everywhere,"}},{"n":81,"text":"अन्वेषमाणा भर्तारं नलं रणविशारदम् ।\nमहात्मानं कृतास्त्रं च विचरामीह दुःखिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"searching for my husband Nala, the great-souled, skilled in battle and in weapons."}},{"n":82,"text":"कच्चिद्भगवतां पुण्यं तपोवनमिदं नृपः ।\nभवेत्प्राप्तो नलो नाम निषधानां जनाधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Has King Nala, lord of the Nishadhas, perhaps come to this holy ascetic forest of yours, blessed ones?"}},{"n":83,"text":"यत्कृतेऽहमिदं विप्राः प्रपन्ना भृशदारुणम् ।\nवनं प्रतिभयं घोरं शार्दूलमृगसेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For his sake I, brahmins, have entered this dreadful, fearsome forest haunted by tigers and beasts."}},{"n":84,"text":"यदि कैश्चिदहोरात्रैर्न द्रक्ष्यामि नलं नृपम् ।\nआत्मानं श्रेयसा योक्ष्ये देहस्यास्य विमोचनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I do not see King Nala within a few days and nights, I will win a better fate by shedding this body."}},{"n":85,"text":"को नु मे जीवितेनार्थस्तमृते पुरुषर्षभम् ।\nकथं भविष्याम्यद्याहं भर्तृशोकाभिपीडिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"What use is life to me without that bull among men? How shall I be today, crushed by grief for my husband?\""}},{"n":86,"text":"एवं विलपतीमेकामरण्ये भीमनन्दिनीम् ।\nदमयन्तीमथोचुस्ते तापसाः सत्यवादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Bhima's daughter lamented thus alone in the forest, those truthful ascetics said to Damayanti:"}},{"n":87,"text":"उदर्कस्तव कल्याणि कल्याणो भविता शुभे ।\nवयं पश्याम तपसा क्षिप्रं द्रक्ष्यसि नैषधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The outcome for you, fair lady, will be good. By our austerity we see that you will soon see the Nishadha."}},{"n":88,"text":"निषधानामधिपतिं नलं रिपुनिघातिनम् ।\nभैमि धर्मभृतां श्रेष्ठं द्रक्ष्यसे विगतज्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You will see Nala, lord of the Nishadhas and slayer of foes, best of the upholders of dharma, free of fever, Bhaimi."}},{"n":89,"text":"विमुक्तं सर्वपापेभ्यः सर्वरत्नसमन्वितम् ।\nतदेव नगरश्रेष्ठं प्रशासन्तमरिंदमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Freed of all sins, endowed with every treasure, ruling that same best of cities, scourge of enemies,"}},{"n":90,"text":"द्विषतां भयकर्तारं सुहृदां शोकनाशनम् ।\nपतिं द्रक्ष्यसि कल्याणि कल्याणाभिजनं नृपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"a cause of fear to foes and destroyer of his friends' sorrow, you will see your husband, fair lady, that king of noble birth.\""}},{"n":91,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा नलस्येष्टां महिषीं पार्थिवात्मजाम् ।\nअन्तर्हितास्तापसास्ते साग्निहोत्राश्रमास्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this to the king's daughter, Nala's beloved queen, the ascetics vanished along with their fire-sacrifice hermitage."}},{"n":92,"text":"सा दृष्ट्वा महदाश्चर्यं विस्मिता अभवत्तदा ।\nदमयन्त्यनवद्याङ्गी वीरसेननृपस्नुषा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing this great wonder, faultless Damayanti, daughter-in-law of King Virasena, was amazed."}},{"n":93,"text":"किं नु स्वप्नो मया दृष्टः कोऽयं विधिरिहाभवत् ।\nक्व नु ते तापसाः सर्वे क्व तदाश्रममण्डलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Did I see a dream? What sort of fate is this? Where are all those ascetics, where is that circle of hermitages?"}},{"n":94,"text":"क्व सा पुण्यजला रम्या नानाद्विजनिषेविता ।\nनदी ते च नगा हृद्याः फलपुष्पोपशोभिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where is that lovely river of sacred water frequented by many birds, and those charming trees adorned with fruit and flowers?\""}},{"n":95,"text":"ध्यात्वा चिरं भीमसुता दमयन्ती शुचिस्मिता ।\nभर्तृशोकपरा दीना विवर्णवदनाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After long reflection, Bhima's daughter Damayanti of pure smile, given over to grief for her husband, became wretched and pale."}},{"n":96,"text":"सा गत्वाथापरां भूमिं बाष्पसंदिग्धया गिरा ।\nविललापाश्रुपूर्णाक्षी दृष्ट्वाशोकतरुं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She went to another place, her words choked with tears, and, eyes full of tears, wept as she saw an ashoka tree."}},{"n":97,"text":"उपगम्य तरुश्रेष्ठमशोकं पुष्पितं तदा ।\nपल्लवापीडितं हृद्यं विहंगैरनुनादितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She approached that finest tree, an ashoka then in bloom, charming with soft young leaves and loud with birds."}},{"n":98,"text":"अहो बतायमगमः श्रीमानस्मिन्वनान्तरे ।\nआपीडैर्बहुभिर्भाति श्रीमान्द्रमिडराडिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Oh, how splendid this tree is in the forest. With its many clusters it shines like a glorious king of Dravida."}},{"n":99,"text":"विशोकां कुरु मां क्षिप्रमशोक प्रियदर्शन ।\nवीतशोकभयाबाधं कच्चित्त्वं दृष्टवान्नृपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashoka, pleasing to see, quickly make me free of sorrow. Have you seen the king, free of sorrow, fear and trouble,"}},{"n":100,"text":"नलं नामारिदमनं दमयन्त्याः प्रियं पतिम् ।\nनिषधानामधिपतिं दृष्टवानसि मे प्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nala, subduer of foes, beloved husband of Damayanti, lord of the Nishadhas, my beloved?"}},{"n":101,"text":"एकवस्त्रार्धसंवीतं सुकुमारतनुत्वचम् ।\nव्यसनेनार्दितं वीरमरण्यमिदमागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wearing half a single garment, with delicate body and skin, afflicted by misfortune, the hero came to this forest."}},{"n":102,"text":"यथा विशोका गच्छेयमशोकनग तत्कुरु ।\nसत्यनामा भवाशोक मम शोकविनाशनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tree, make it so that I may go free of sorrow. Be true to your name, Ashoka, by destroying my sorrow.\""}},{"n":103,"text":"एवं साशोकवृक्षं तमार्ता त्रिः परिगम्य ह ।\nजगाम दारुणतरं देशं भैमी वराङ्गना ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, afflicted, she circled that ashoka tree three times and went on to a still more terrible region, Bhima's daughter, fine of limb."}},{"n":104,"text":"सा ददर्श नगान्नैकान्नैकाश्च सरितस्तथा ।\nनैकांश्च पर्वतान्रम्यान्नैकांश्च मृगपक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She saw many trees, many rivers, many lovely mountains and many animals and birds."}},{"n":105,"text":"कन्दरांश्च नितम्बांश्च नदांश्चाद्भुतदर्शनान् ।\nददर्श सा भीमसुता पतिमन्वेषती तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"She saw caves, hillsides and wonderful-looking torrents, Bhima's daughter, searching for her husband then."}},{"n":106,"text":"गत्वा प्रकृष्टमध्वानं दमयन्ती शुचिस्मिता ।\nददर्शाथ महासार्थं हस्त्यश्वरथसंकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After going far along the road, Damayanti of pure smile saw a great caravan crowded with elephants, horses and chariots."}},{"n":107,"text":"उत्तरन्तं नदीं रम्यां प्रसन्नसलिलां शुभाम् ।\nसुशीततोयां विस्तीर्णां ह्रदिनीं वेतसैर्वृताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was crossing a lovely, beautiful river with clear water, very cool, broad, edged with reeds,"}},{"n":108,"text":"प्रोद्घुष्टां क्रौञ्चकुररैश्चक्रवाकोपकूजिताम् ।\nकूर्मग्राहझषाकीर्णां पुलिनद्वीपशोभिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"loud with curlews and ospreys, humming with chakravaka birds, filled with turtles, crocodiles and fish, adorned with sandbanks and islets."}},{"n":109,"text":"सा दृष्ट्वैव महासार्थं नलपत्नी यशस्विनी ।\nउपसर्प्य वरारोहा जनमध्यं विवेश ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that large caravan, the famed wife of Nala drew near and entered among the people."}},{"n":110,"text":"उन्मत्तरूपा शोकार्ता तथा वस्त्रार्धसंवृता ।\nकृशा विवर्णा मलिना पांसुध्वस्तशिरोरुहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Looking like a madwoman, grieving, wearing half a garment, thin, pale, dirty, her hair covered in dust,"}},{"n":111,"text":"तां दृष्ट्वा तत्र मनुजाः केचिद्भीताः प्रदुद्रुवुः ।\nकेचिच्चिन्तापरास्तस्थुः केचित्तत्र विचुक्रुशुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"when people there saw her, some ran away in fear, some stood thinking, and some cried out."}},{"n":112,"text":"प्रहसन्ति स्म तां केचिदभ्यसूयन्त चापरे ।\nचक्रुस्तस्यां दयां केचित्पप्रच्छुश्चापि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some laughed at her, some scorned her, some pitied her, and some questioned her, Bharata."}},{"n":113,"text":"कासि कस्यासि कल्याणि किं वा मृगयसे वने ।\nत्वां दृष्ट्वा व्यथिताः स्मेह कच्चित्त्वमसि मानुषी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who are you and whose, good lady, and what do you seek in the forest? We are shaken seeing you; are you a human woman?"}},{"n":114,"text":"वद सत्यं वनस्यास्य पर्वतस्याथ वा दिशः ।\nदेवता त्वं हि कल्याणि त्वां वयं शरणं गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell us the truth: are you the goddess of this forest, or this mountain, or some direction? We have come to you for refuge."}},{"n":115,"text":"यक्षी वा राक्षसी वा त्वमुताहोऽसि वराङ्गना ।\nसर्वथा कुरु नः स्वस्ति रक्षस्वास्माननिन्दिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Are you a yakshi, a rakshasi or a fine woman? In every way give us good fortune and protect us, blameless one."}},{"n":116,"text":"यथायं सर्वथा सार्थः क्षेमी शीघ्रमितो व्रजेत् ।\nतथा विधत्स्व कल्याणि त्वां वयं शरणं गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arrange, fair lady, that this caravan may go safely from here soon; we have come to you for refuge.\""}},{"n":117,"text":"तथोक्ता तेन सार्थेन दमयन्ती नृपात्मजा ।\nप्रत्युवाच ततः साध्वी भर्तृव्यसनदुःखिता ।\nसार्थवाहं च सार्थं च जना ये चात्र केचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to thus by the caravan, King's daughter Damayanti, devoted and sorrowing over her husband's misfortune, answered, addressing the caravan leader, the caravan and all the people there:"}},{"n":118,"text":"यूनः स्थविरबालाश्च सार्थस्य च पुरोगमाः ।\nमानुषीं मां विजानीत मनुजाधिपतेः सुताम् ।\nनृपस्नुषां राजभार्यां भर्तृदर्शनलालसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Young men, old men, children and you who lead the caravan, know me as a human, a daughter of a king, a king's daughter-in-law and a king's wife, eager to see my husband."}},{"n":119,"text":"विदर्भराण्मम पिता भर्ता राजा च नैषधः ।\nनलो नाम महाभागस्तं मार्गाम्यपराजितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of Vidarbha is my father, and my husband is the Nishadha king, the greatly fortunate Nala; I am searching for that invincible man."}},{"n":120,"text":"यदि जानीत नृपतिं क्षिप्रं शंसत मे प्रियम् ।\nनलं पार्थिवशार्दूलममित्रगणसूदनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you know of that king, tell me quickly the good news of my beloved Nala, tiger among kings and slayer of hosts of enemies.\""}},{"n":121,"text":"तामुवाचानवद्याङ्गीं सार्थस्य महतः प्रभुः ।\nसार्थवाहः शुचिर्नाम शृणु कल्याणि मद्वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great caravan's leader, named Shuchi, said to the faultless lady: \"Listen, good lady, to my words."}},{"n":122,"text":"अहं सार्थस्य नेता वै सार्थवाहः शुचिस्मिते ।\nमनुष्यं नलनामानं न पश्यामि यशस्विनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am the leader of this caravan, a merchant, lady of pure smile. I have not seen any man named Nala, famed one."}},{"n":123,"text":"कुञ्जरद्वीपिमहिषशार्दूलर्क्षमृगानपि ।\nपश्याम्यस्मिन्वने कष्टे अमनुष्यनिषेविते ।\nतथा नो यक्षराडद्य मणिभद्रः प्रसीदतु ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see elephants, leopards, buffalo, tigers, bears and deer in this difficult forest, which no men inhabit. So may Manibhadra, king of yakshas, be gracious to us today.\""}},{"n":124,"text":"साब्रवीद्वणिजः सर्वान्सार्थवाहं च तं ततः ।\nक्व नु यास्यसि सार्थोऽयमेतदाख्यातुमर्हथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"She asked all the merchants and that leader: \"Where will this caravan go? Please tell me.\""}},{"text":"सार्थवाह उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The caravan leader said:"}},{"n":125,"text":"सार्थोऽयं चेदिराजस्य सुबाहोः सत्यवादिनः ।\nक्षिप्रं जनपदं गन्ता लाभाय मनुजात्मजे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This caravan, daughter of man, belongs to Subahu, the truthful king of Chedi, and will quickly go to that country for trade.\""}}]}]}